.TH CCOL_CHAN_TRY_RECV_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_try_recv_zc \- try to receive a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_try_recv_zc(ccol_channel *ch, c_message_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Takes a message from the queue that the channel picks for the calling
thread, if one is there, and returns at once when that queue is empty.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch          Channel to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - A message was received. The caller must free
                       target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args    - ch or target_buf is NULL
ccol_container_empty - The chosen queue is empty
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This call never blocks. The direction comes from the ID of the
calling thread, as described in ccol_chan_recv_zc(3).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_timed_recv_zc (3)
